    "bilayer_cpu200_legacy_admission_finding": {
      "primary_source": "research_20261010/bilayer_cpu200_legacy_admission_finding/REVIEW.md",
      "source_sha256": "08ff48ce9e920252f478df3904b252f3bc5e05b4ebbf411ea74800d193d9ef12",
      "verdict": "# Static correction: legacy 20,000 threshold blocks completion\n\n2026-10-11 06:28 UTC /02:28 EDT. Full-run readiness FAIL pending a separately authorized remedy. This is a new finding; all existing sealed checkpoint and source reviews remain unchanged. Their exact partial scientific data and tested component results remain valid, but their continuation-readiness conclusions need this correction.\n\nFrozen source: `bilayer_outer_cpu200_revision`, manifest `064a67a28aadc63998b4590b35362da0a86fa9f4fcb519c768b7c4f32ac1c78c`. File `physical_session.py`, SHA256 `8903151362c65c9577b6a60abaac6f65dba4521e88246277bacf852e2f578ada`. Job `25dec9c509f16764b2f7f9cf9207ad8e1297aa644d83b96d09ddb36b7d1fe4db`.\n\nThe dispatcher checks both the valid complete forecast and this additional legacy assertion before every worker:\n\n`assert CONTROL_POOL + store.worker_charged + row['cap'] <= 20000`\n\nThe approved partition is standard16,800 +control2,300 +retry2,500 =21,600. The new clean generation already includes1,968 retired worker charges. Full completion therefore needs2,300+1,968+16,800=21,068 in the legacy left side, exceeding20,000. The independently reviewed21,600 full-forecast expression does not bypass this second assertion.\n\nWithout retries, the first290 chunks reserve870 standard seconds. At most2,477 q6 chunks then fit:870+2,477*6=15,732 standard. Thus2,767 chunks can complete before the next row (zero-based2767) would require20,006 and fail before reserving that worker. The remaining178 q6 chunks cannot be admitted. Earlier actual failures or stops may of course occur first.\n\nThe prior source review correctly found the physical dispatcher byte-identical, but did not evaluate this inherited resource assertion across the entire new partition/carry plan. Source identity alone is insufficient for a changed budget. The reviewer informed root and producer immediately after identifying it. No new scientific work, source mutation, launch, retry or budget expansion was performed for this finding. Existing all24-field data are unaffected by this admission-only issue.\n\nRoot must decide a safe stop and any source/job/receipt-identity repair. A remedy must preserve all actual charges and prior source/receipt identities, include a metadata walk through all2,945 admissions under the intended carry, and obtain new independent review and explicit launch authority. This finding does not authorize an in-place patch or silent adoption.\n"
    },
