    "bilayer_supervisor10_migration_review": {
      "primary_source": "research_20261010/bilayer_supervisor10_migration_review/FAILED_REVIEW.md",
      "source_sha256": "a2ed813adeb1bdde0902a827832c4ae1e7487fd3c2c0c48deb98e455ee36b4ad",
      "verdict": "# Preserved independent-review interruption\n\nThe single authorized 60-CPU metadata review stopped on a reviewer harness assertion. It did not reach the fresh startup, supervisor fault or memory tests. No physical worker ran and no retry occurred.\n\n`check_review.py` line81 incorrectly required the successor carry ledger to equal the predecessor's live ledger verbatim. The predecessor correctly remains at prepaid2,800, reserved2,541,52 sessions. The successor carry explicitly preserves those52 records, changes the approved control pool to4,200 and appends the authorized60 metadata-gate record, reaching reserved2,601 and53 records. This is the intended no-refund accounting, not a producer carry defect.\n\nThe traceback occurred after the source/pin checks, producer recursive origin validation and independent loops over all2,263 current origin chains plus852 ancestor chains. Those loops checked9,345 canonical byte bindings and54,312 signed accumulator values with original raw receipts, target schedules and exact chunk assembly. They also checked new-envelope equality, coverage1/496/4495/126272, the retained failed6 reservation, and absence of an accepted commit for row2263. This is evidence from the completed deterministic prefix; the final import archive comparison, planned fault tests and overall acceptance did not run. No whole-gate PASS is asserted.\n\nObserved child-tree wait4 CPU16.474532 seconds, guard CPU0.357416, wall17.792001, sampled total RSS60,678,144 bytes. Exit1; no guard stop reason, orphans or survivors. The entire60-second reservation remains charged. Any correction/completion requires a new explicit root decision. The producer source seal103aaf4dffb99f4bd89abb2ce13fad6d48220ec341c36e9d3add3793fbfbb366 remains unchanged.\n\nPublication preserves the failed checker, guard/helpers, logs, reservation, proposed inputs and frozen source/archive copy. The extracted duplicate tree is retained locally but excluded from the manifest; its original archive and member manifest are included under source/.\n"
    },
    "bilayer_supervisor10_migration_review_completion": {
      "primary_source": "research_20261010/bilayer_supervisor10_migration_review_completion/PARTIAL_REVIEW.md",
      "source_sha256": "7a7211a0947b1f723176fe97056e4f496ae2f963a509e63a13ce13f8cc1bf106",
      "verdict": "# Preserved bounded completion\n\nStatus: component checks passed; whole review incomplete. The authorized completion remained within the original 60-second charge and stopped at its aggregate CPU guard. No physical worker ran.\n\nCompleted: all 2,263 origin chains plus 852 ancestor chains, 9,345 canonical byte bindings, 54,312 signed values, exact new envelopes, failed row 2263 charge retention, corrected carry 2,601 control and 14,682 worker, interrupted-import recovery, idempotence, coherent corruption/noncanonical-byte rejection, all 2,945 admission prefixes, actual final 32-pin startup cutpoints, nested resource inheritance, and normal/controller-death/accounting-failure/synthetic-overage diagnostic tests. The synthetic overage value 10.25 is explicitly injected, not measured CPU.\n\nThe real cleanup fixture received the graceful-stop signal but the outer review guard stopped the whole tree before its 8-second supervisor cleanup point. No final diagnostic from this fixture exists. Fresh full-shape concurrent stress and observer rejection checks had not started. No implementation assertion failed. A separate decision is required to finish those tests.\n\nCompletion tree wait4 29.079128 CPU seconds, guard .663063, wall 34.421715, sampled aggregate RSS 100,106,240 bytes. Direct exit -9; one killed fixture descendant was reaped by the guard, no survivor. Stop reason aggregate_process_tree_CPU_guard. Prior attempt 16.474532 tree + .357416 guard, total observed test CPU 46.574139. Full original 60 remains charged; no second charge was created by this completion. Source seal 103aaf4dffb99f4bd89abb2ce13fad6d48220ec341c36e9d3add3793fbfbb366 is unchanged.\n\nThe origin_extracted symlink points to the previously sealed archive extraction, whose members were fully rehashed in this attempt. The generated NONPHYSICAL_IMPORT_FIXTURE is retained locally but excluded from publication; it is reproducible from the pinned checker and source archives. It is never eligible for physical coverage. The manifest covers the checker, source/archive copy, diagnostics, ledgers and summary evidence.\n"
    },
    "bilayer_supervisor10_remaining_tests_review": {
      "primary_source": "research_20261010/bilayer_supervisor10_remaining_tests_review/PARTIAL_REVIEW.md",
      "source_sha256": "cb8b8a4f83e9248c75a5aae1e2f80575c6021eec84afdcdfcf04385a61c4cc2d",
      "verdict": "# Remaining-test evidence and harness interruption\n\nThe fresh actual-CPU supervisor cleanup passed: graceful signal at 5.006335 CPU seconds, diagnostic cleanup at 8.008122, child killed/reaped, inherited lock checked, no survivor. The 2,945-record nonphysical controller/store/final-JSON stress and 3,035-observation outer serialization also passed together with all five actual role CPU/AS profiles. Controller VmPeak 76,054,528 bytes under AS128 MiB; outer 61,632,512. Synthetic values have 128 digits in all 24 fields; first 852 records carry the extra ancestral envelope. The synthetic native role only allocates 64 MiB and executes no physics.\n\nThe checker then failed importing engine into the isolated observer module because the reviewer omitted the frozen source directory from sys.path. The observer rejection checks therefore did not run. No producer assertion failed. All children had been reaped before this error. Tree wait4 11.437730 CPU seconds, guard .250289, wall 12.071499, sampled aggregate RSS197,390,336 bytes, exit1, no guard stop reason or survivors. Full separate20 charge is retained, in addition to the previous closed60 charge. Whole gate remains incomplete until the observer-only correction is explicitly authorized and passes.\n\nGenerated stress/SYNTHETIC_NONPHYSICAL_2945 metadata files and the origin extraction symlink are retained locally but excluded from the publication manifest. Synthetic final output, full outer serialization, READY role observations, code, logs, resource receipts and diagnostics are included. These nonphysical data cannot enter physical coverage.\n"
    },
